## 1. Typical Exam Question: "What are the core components of an explosive system?"
In engineering and applied sciences, a conventional blasting system is divided into components based on their function in the explosive train (the sequence of steps that leads to detonation):

* 
* The Initiator (Fuze/Trigger): The component that provides the initial stimulus (mechanical, electrical, or thermal) to start the reaction.
* The Primary Explosive (Detonator/Primer): A highly sensitive compound used in small amounts. It converts the small stimulus from the trigger into a sharp, high-velocity shockwave.
* The Secondary Explosive (Main Charge): A stable, insensitive compound that makes up the bulk of the device. It requires the intense shockwave from the detonator to react. It will not detonate from simple heat or friction.
